CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*map)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct tsi721_ib_win_mapping)...)
#83: FILE: drivers/rapidio/devices/tsi721.c:918:
+		map = kzalloc(sizeof(struct tsi721_ib_win_mapping), GFP_ATOMIC);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!map"
#84: FILE: drivers/rapidio/devices/tsi721.c:919:
+		if (map == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

